    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vŏmĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		vomo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a spewing</i>, <i>vomiting.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 2, 50, 126</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 53, 117, § 282</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">21, 20, 83, §
				144</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22, 25,
				64, § 132</span></i>; 26, 7, 25, § 41
			al.—Collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vŏmĭtĭum</span></b> ,
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2, §
			136</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, concr., <i>that which
				is vomited</i>, <i>a vomit</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">varii colores vomitionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					25, 5, 23, § 57</span></i>
			.</div>
